Package: ccat-cx9240-dkms
Version: 1.0-7
Architecture: all
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: CX9240 bench build <root@localhost>
Depends: dkms (>= 2.1.0.0), linux-headers-bhf, gcc, make, kmod, iproute2
Conflicts: tc31-xar-um
Description: Linux netdev driver for the Beckhoff CX9240 internal EtherCAT master, with UPS support files
 Enables the CX9240's internal EtherCAT master (CCAT FPGA function 0x14 at
 0xA0020000) and exposes it as network interface eth0, so a Linux EtherCAT
 master such as CODESYS Control can drive the EL terminals without TwinCAT.
 Based on the public Beckhoff CCAT driver plus a reverse-engineered enable
 sequence and platform DMA wiring (16 MB aligned DMA bases).
 .
 Needs the kernel headers of the running kernel (linux-headers-*-bhf) and
 about 64 MB of free CMA memory. Verified only on one CX9240 with an EL2008.
